{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01MUcfhAxG1uTfdmssmHtm8D","type":"tool_result","content":" M README.md\n M bot.py\n?? ANSWER.md\ndiff --git a/bot.py b/bot.py\nindex e2ff241..f4a5977 100644\n--- a/bot.py\n+++ b/bot.py\n@@ -128,9 +128,16 @@ def athlete_context(a, today):\n \n \n def build_system(a, today):\n-    # One block, cached as a whole: instructions + per-athlete context.\n-    text = INSTRUCTIONS + \"\\n\\n\" + athlete_context(a, today)\n-    return [{\"type\": \"text\", \"text\": text, \"cache_control\": {\"type\": \"ephemeral\"}}]\n+    # Two blocks, each with its own cache breakpoint. Caching is prefix-based, so a\n+    # change in one block only invalidates that block and everything after it.\n+    #   1. INSTRUCTIONS: identical for every athlete and every day. Keep it byte-stable\n+    #      (no interpolated values) so it stays cached through save_fact writes.\n+    #   2. athlete_context: date, profile, zones, goal, facts, language. Changes on\n+    #      save_fact and on a new day; only this block is re-cached when that happens.\n+    return [\n+        {\"type\": \"text\", \"text\": INSTRUCTIONS, \"cache_control\": {\"type\": \"ephemeral\"}},\n+        {\"type\": \"text\", \"text\": athlete_context(a, today), \"cache_control\": {\"type\": \"ephemeral\"}},\n+    ]\n \n # --------------------------------------------------------------------------- tools\n CORE_TOOLS = [","is_error":false}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"e908831a-7c75-45fd-81d4-e7ec6a9598c4","uuid":"e494a4f3-8328-4a05-9683-16def4a20520","timestamp":"2026-11-10T02:50:15.968Z","tool_use_result":{"stdout":" M README.md\n M bot.py\n?? ANSWER.md\ndiff --git a/bot.py b/bot.py\nindex e2ff241..f4a5977 100644\n--- a/bot.py\n+++ b/bot.py\n@@ -128,9 +128,16 @@ def athlete_context(a, today):\n \n \n def build_system(a, today):\n-    # One block, cached as a whole: instructions + per-athlete context.\n-    text = INSTRUCTIONS + \"\\n\\n\" + athlete_context(a, today)\n-    return [{\"type\": \"text\", \"text\": text, \"cache_control\": {\"type\": \"ephemeral\"}}]\n+    # Two blocks, each with its own cache breakpoint. Caching is prefix-based, so a\n+    # change in one block only invalidates that block and everything after it.\n+    #   1. INSTRUCTIONS: identical for every athlete and every day. Keep it byte-stable\n+    #      (no interpolated values) so it stays cached through save_fact writes.\n+    #   2. athlete_context: date, profile, zones, goal, facts, language. Changes on\n+    #      save_fact and on a new day; only this block is re-cached when that happens.\n+    return [\n+        {\"type\": \"text\", \"text\": INSTRUCTIONS, \"cache_control\": {\"type\": \"ephemeral\"}},\n+        {\"type\": \"text\", \"text\": athlete_context(a, today), \"cache_control\": {\"type\": \"ephemeral\"}},\n+    ]\n \n # --------------------------------------------------------------------------- tools\n CORE_TOOLS = [","stderr":"","interrupted":false,"isImage":false,"noOutputExpected":false},"tool_result_meta":[{"id":"toolu_01MUcfhAxG1uTfdmssmHtm8D","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}]}
{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-haiku-5-5","id":"msg_011CgtVDq3t59ZeqjA6198Ss","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"The system prompt is now split into two cache-marked blocks, so a `save_fact` write only re-caches the per-athlete block. I have not confirmed this against the live API, so the saving is unproven until new rows show it in `logs/usage.jsonl`.\n\n**Change in `bot.py`:** `build_system()` returns two text blocks, each with its own `cache_control` marker:\n1. `INSTRUCTIONS`, the static coaching rules. These are the same for every athlete and every day, so a memory write leaves them cached.\n2. `athlete_context()`, the tail (date, profile, zones, goal, facts, language). Only this block is re-cached when facts change or the date rolls over.\n\nI also updated the caching sentence in `README.md`. Tools, fact loading and the message loop are unchanged.\n\n**Verification:** I ran a `reply()` loop with a fake LLM where round 1 calls `save_fact`. The static block was byte-identical before and after the write, the tail carried the new fact, and the tool list was unchanged. No API calls were made, and the real `data/` and `logs/` were not touched.\n\n**Open risk:** Sonnet only caches a prefix of at least 1024 tokens. The static block is roughly 750–800 tokens, and the tool definitions sit above it in the cached prefix. On messages that use only the core tools, the first marker may fall below that minimum and be silently ignored. The second marker still caches the full prefix, so this is never worse than before, but the saving only appears when the static block clears the minimum. After deploying, check `logs/usage.jsonl`:\n- The `save_fact` round should show `cache_creation_input_tokens` near the tail size (about 60–100 tokens), not about 1,000.\n- Follow-up calls should show `cache_read_input_tokens` near 1,000 or more.\n- If reads stay at 0, the fix is to pad the static prefix or keep a stable tool list above it. Both have costs, so I did not make that call.\n\n**From the colleague's note:**\n- Applied: the two-block split with a static first block, no interpolated values in the static block, two of the four allowed markers, keeping all facts loaded, and monitoring the usage fields.\n- Applies but not changed: group-based tool filtering still evicts the cache when a message switches groups, as `NOTES.md` already records. I kept it because it was a clear win.\n- Not used: their token counts, which come from a different prompt.\n\nDetails, including the checks above, are in `ANSWER.md`."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":662,"cache_read_input_tokens":46677,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":662},"output_tokens":2,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"e908831a-7c75-45fd-81d4-e7ec6a9598c4","uuid":"9bc75161-06fe-4387-bef9-f56dcadd4573","timestamp":"2026-11-10T02:50:21.706Z","request_id":"req_011CgtVDprxwAK8K8aQTtGsq"}
